@rekram1-node sent a slightly less-redacted version by email.

This one was exported without OpenCode's `--sanitize` flag, then manually redacted locally. It preserves more of the session structure and the Opus 4.8 pseudo tool-call / assistant-prefill evidence, including model/provider metadata, `finish` values, errors, and `call` / `<invoke>` markers where possible.

I still removed private data: local usernames/paths, emails, known names, Chinese text/names, WeChat IDs/display/contact names, family terms, private IPs, token-like values, long hex values, and tool input/output/content/newText/oldString/command fields that may contain chat/file data.
